// name :
"P492614155" "The Fire and The Flames"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SoulCatcherClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1263072237" "Mortimer Kal's Soul Catcher"
// DetailString :
"P1440638491" "This object is about the size of a bowling pin and appears to be chipped from a single massive shard of crystal. It isn't ruby, garnet, or any quartz you've ever seen, but it is blood red and extraordinarily cool to the touch. The gem appears to be hollow in the middle, or perhaps it is a trick of the light. Whatever the case, its purpose has been made clear to you by Mortimer Kal. This shard focuses eldritch energy and draws the soul of one unlucky individual into it, trapping them. You have no idea if there is a way to let a captured soul free."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NuminasSoulClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3091250180" "Numina's Soul"
// DetailString :
"P880515565" "You have captured Numina's soul within the Soul Catcher. The interior of the ruddy gem is clouded and when you think of Numina you can hear her quietly weeping and bemoaning the bitter cold and alienation from all that is living. When you speak her name she immediately responds and asks how she might serve you in order to gain release from her hellish prison.<br><br>This makes you smile."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FistsOfVulcanClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1772055932" "The Fists of Vulcan"
// DetailString :
"P3730123473" "These mighty gauntlets appear to be forged from cast iron and are cold to the touch. However, when you put them on a living flame erupts from the hands, promising to melt anything it touches except for the bearer. Could these truly have been the gloves worn by the god of the forge and used to smith the weapons of the gods? Only by seizing the Flames of Prometheus will you discover whether the legend is indeed true. Until then, you will store them safely out of sight so as to avoid attention and that bounty that Odysseus put on your head."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ShatteredSoulCatcherClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2567506935" "The Shattered Soul Catcher"
// DetailString :
"P1128712592" "A pile of red dust and broken shards of crystal are all that remain of Mortimer Kal's Soul Catcher after Numina escaped its hellish prison. You aren't sure exactly what caused it to break. Perhaps it was destroyed by the power of the Flames of Prometheus, like the Fists of Vulcan were, or maybe... just maybe... it was... love?<br><br>Nah, it must have been the Flames of Prometheus."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FistsOfAshClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1254155818" "Fistfuls of Ash"
// DetailString :
"P1802887320" "After handling the Flames of Prometheus with the Fists of Vulcan the power of the flames reduced the once glorious magical artifacts to only a fistful of ash."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3106298633" "The Flame of Prometheus"
// DetailString :
"P248895173" "The Rogue Isles have been awash in chaos ever since the power of the incarnates started to manifest. You wanted a piece of that power pie for yourself, but that nerd in Ouroboros, Ramiel, wouldn't confide in you the great secret. As usual, you were on your own, so you went back to basics and kidnapped someone who could help you, or rather, the loved one of someone who could help you; a young girl by the name of Fiona Kal.<br><br>Pissing off Mortimer Kal was as bold a move as any you've ever undertaken. As a powerful sorcerer within the Midnight Squad, most people would assume that messing with his family meant a grisly and indescribable doom, but you had learned his secret weakness. Fiona was all that Mortimer had left to hold onto in this world, and threatening that meant you had him by the proverbial crystal balls.<br><br>With Fiona safely hidden away, you confronted Mortimer with your offer; use his wizardly ways to discover a means of you obtaining incarnate power or Fiona would be sent back to him in pieces too mangled to be properly resurrected. The wizard buckled like a belt and vowed to do anything to keep his daughter alive. He proved most helpful, and laid out a plan to steal the Flames of Prometheus; a spark of incarnate power in the possession of someone Mortimer assured you was undeserving of it; Positron.<br><br>The first step was to sucker punch the Freedom Phalanx right in their magical soft spot; Numina. This would throw the Phalanx off balance and, by using Mortimer Kal's Soul Catcher to imprison her, you would gain access to Positron's Lab, where the Flames of Prometheus were kept. With Numina in your possession the Phalanx would be blind to your sorcerous scheme."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2521298948" "The Rogue Isles have been awash in chaos ever since the power of the incarnates started to manifest. You wanted a piece of that power pie for yourself, but that nerd in Ouroboros, Ramiel, wouldn't confide in you the great secret. As usual, you were on your own, so you went back to basics and kidnapped someone who could help you, or rather, the loved one of someone who could help you; a young girl by the name of Fiona Kal.<br><br>Pissing off Mortimer Kal was as bold a move as any you've ever undertaken. As a powerful sorcerer within the Midnight Squad, most people would assume that messing with his family meant a grisly and indescribable doom, but you had learned his secret weakness. Fiona was all that Mortimer had left to hold onto in this world, and threatening that meant you had him by the proverbial crystal balls.<br><br>With Fiona safely hidden away, you confronted Mortimer with your offer; use his wizardly ways to discover a means of you obtaining incarnate power or Fiona would be sent back to him in pieces too mangled to be properly resurrected. The wizard buckled like a belt and vowed to do anything to keep his daughter alive. He proved most helpful, and laid out a plan to steal the Flames of Prometheus; a spark of incarnate power in the possession of someone Mortimer assured you was undeserving of it; Positron.<br><br>The first step was to sucker punch the Freedom Phalanx right in their magical soft spot; Numina. This would throw the Phalanx off balance and, by using Mortimer Kal's Soul Catcher to imprison her, you would gain access to Positron's Lab, where the Flames of Prometheus were kept. With Numina in your possession the Phalanx would be blind to your sorcerous scheme.<br><br>But capturing Numina was only the first part of the plan. You had the key to gaining access Positron's Lab, but the Flames of Prometheus were power beyond what mere mortals could possess and could not simply be picked up and carried off, for they would consume you body and soul. To safely acquire the Flames you would need more magical power, and this time it was in the possession of Paragon City's greatest trafficker in ancient artifacts; David Odysseus Hill. The playboy leader of The Warriors had used his family's shipping empire to squirrel away artifacts from around the globe, and in his possession was an artifact capable of touching the Flames of Prometheus; the Fists of Vulcan. Breaking into Odysseus's warehouse would have been a lot simpler of an affair if the Midnight Squad hadn't guessed at your plan. They sought to ambush you and take you down, but when the smoke cleared you had shown them what for. Your plan, however, did not go unnoticed by the treacherous Darrin Wade, and he warned Odysseus of your plans to rob him. He arrived none-too-pleased. Ultimately, however, even he and his Warriors stood no chance against you and your destiny."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - MortimerKalSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P666535701" "You can feel the Flame of Prometheus burning within you every time you enter battle, and whenever you finish a fight, you can feel its power smouldering just beneath the surface. You cannot help but reflect upon your daring plan to steal this power and that to achieve it you were ready to brave...<br><br><b>The Fire and the Flames</b><br><br>The Rogue Isles have been awash in chaos ever since the power of the incarnates started to manifest. You wanted a piece of that power pie for yourself, but that nerd in Ouroboros, Ramiel, wouldn't confide in you the great secret. As usual, you were on your own, so you went back to basics and kidnapped someone who could help you, or rather, the loved one of someone who could help you; Fiona Kal.<br><br>Pissing off Mortimer Kal was as bold a move as any you've ever undertaken. As a powerful sorcerer within the Midnight Squad, most people would assume that messing with his family meant a grisly and indescribable doom, but you had learned his secret weakness. Fiona was all that Mortimer had left to hold onto in this world, and threatening that meant you had him by the proverbial crystal balls.<br><br>With Fiona safely hidden away, you confronted Mortimer with your offer; use his wizardly ways to discover a means of you obtaining incarnate power or Fiona would be sent back to him in pieces too mangled to be properly resurrected. The wizard buckled like a belt and vowed to do anything to keep his daughter alive. He proved most helpful, and laid out a plan to steal the Flames of Prometheus; a spark of incarnate power in the possession of someone Mortimer assured you was undeserving of it; Positron.<br><br>The first step was to sucker punch the Freedom Phalanx right in their magical soft spot; Numina. This would throw the Phalanx off balance and, by using Mortimer Kal's Soul Catcher to imprison her, you would gain access to Positron's Lab, where the Flames of Prometheus were kept. With Numina in your possession the Phalanx would be blind to your sorcerous scheme.<br><br>But capturing Numina was only the first part of the plan. You had the key to gaining access Positron's Lab, but the Flames of Prometheus were power beyond what mere mortals could possess and could not simply be picked up and carried off, for they would consume you body and soul. To safely acquire the Flames you would need more magical power, and this time it was in the possession of Paragon City's greatest trafficker in ancient artifacts; David Odysseus Hill. The playboy leader of The Warriors had used his family's shipping empire to squirrel away artifacts from around the globe, and in his possession was an artifact capable of touching the Flames of Prometheus; the Fists of Vulcan. Breaking into Odysseus's warehouse would have been a lot simpler of an affair if the Midnight Squad hadn't guessed at your plan. They sought to ambush you and take you down, but when the smoke cleared you had shown them what for. Your plan, however, did not go unnoticed by the treacherous Darrin Wade, and he warned Odysseus of your plans to rob him. He arrived none-too-pleased. Ultimately, however, even he and his Warriors stood no chance against you and your destiny.<br><br>With the Fists of Vulcan in hand and Numina as the key to entering Positron's Lab, everything was going according to plan, until Positron's security systems alerted him to your presence and he crashed the party. Unfortunately for Posi, he let his feelings get in the way. He offered to let you go in exchange for Numina, but with the power of the Flames already in your possession you saw no reason to entertain any demands except your own. You taught Positron a valuable lesson that day, that love is a weakness to be exploited. The prize was the Flames of Prometheus. Unfortunately, the presence of the Flames had a profound effect on the Soul Catcher, and it fractured, allowing Numina to escape and whisk herself and Positron to safety. Additionally, the Fists of Vulcan were consumed, leaving your hands coated in blackened ash. Despite these losses the power of the Flames is yours! You suspect that your next run in with the Freedom Phalanx will be a heated affair."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - FionaAndMortimerKalSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2515571914" "Fiona and Mortimer Kal"
// tDetailString :
"P2195229409" "Mortimer Kal is a powerful wizard whose loyalty to you hinges on the continued captivity of his daughter, Fiona. You kidnapped young Fiona from the Cap Au Diable University when you discovered that her father was none other than the powerful wizard in your current employ. You discovered that Fiona's father had left her and her mother at a young age, but she was clueless of why. She has harbored cynicism and anger toward her father for all these years and has no clue that her father is both a powerful wizard and has since come to cherish her alone in this world. That he is now your servant because of love unreturned is a bitter joke that you alone enjoy.<br><br>In the meantime, Fiona has come to enjoy what she calls, 'her new diggs' back at your lair. She has even expressed some interest in learning a thing or two about proper villainy.<br><br>Her father, meanwhile, toils for you in all things arcane, ensuring that Numina, Odysseus, and the Midnighters cannot get the drop on you via magical means. His singular drive to keep you happy and ensure his daughter's safety has made him incredibly easy to manage. Were he to learn of how little danger Fiona is truly in you aren't sure if he would summon up all the powers in the cosmos to destroy you on the spot, or cement his loyalty to you even further.<br><br>That, however, is a risk not worth the reward at this time. For now, your thoughts rest on more important matters; like trying to take over the world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Mission1DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P737819950" "Whenever you and your lackeys are ready I will transport you through a doorway of shadows into the subterranean city of Oranbega.<br><br><color orange>Mortimer regards you with minor contempt.</color><br><br>Don't worry, you have my daughter, so I wouldn't dream of shifting you into, say, Ghlar Shodan, the Prison of Slime...<br><br>Remember, Numina does not travel alone, she travels with Infernal. Remember, part of his true name is K'Varr and that there is power in one's true name. With his you will have some power over him."
// Answer Text :
"P3548061234" "I'm ready, wizard. Now send me to Oranbega."
// Answer Text :
"P1826991797" "Patience, wizard. When I'm ready you'll know. (Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TophDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page IntroPage Text :
"P4247266451" "I am Toph Osir, Magus of this district of our glorious city.<br><br>You are not here on the same mission as Numina and her pet, Infernal... what is it you seek? Perhaps I can grant what you wish in exchange for your assistance against that witch, Numina?"
// Answer Text :
"P4192209039" "Fate would have it that it is Numina who I am after."
// Page NuminaPage Text :
"P177603708" "So it would seem that the threads of Fate have brought us together.<br><br>Numina has been using her magic to turn my people against each other. Normally this would pose little problem for our daemons to handle, but that accursed Infernal is with her, and what daemons we have sent against them have been bound within his armor.<br><br>If we could but separate one from the other then both would fall."
// Answer Text :
"P2199733523" "Mortimer Kal said that the name K'Varr might come in handy."
// Page InfernalPage Text :
"P2438984320" "<color orange>Toph Osir scowls at the name of Mortimer Kal, but then his mouth hangs agape at the name of K'Varr.</color><br><br>"Of course! K'Varr is part of Infernal's true name. It isn't absolute power over him, but it is enough to summon him away from his mistress and to a place where he can be bound.<br><br>Once we have Infernal imprisoned I will leave Numina to your capable hands.""
// Answer Text :
"P2172178219" "You have yourself a deal, Toph Osir."
// Page DealPage Text :
"P3977377842" "<color orange>Toph Osir begins chanting a ritual using the name 'K'Varr'.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1517400020" "Leave"
// Page InfernalImprisonedPage Text :
"P127007537" "With Infernal bound by his name and my spell, Numina should prove no threat to you. Once you have dealt with her return to me and I will grant you safe passage from our city.<br><br>But, if I find that your true motive is to steal from my people, then know that there is no respite for thieves within the hallowed walls of Oranbega."
// Answer Text :
"P608101568" "You have nothing of value to me, sorcerer. Numina is my prize."
// Page BetrayalPage Text :
"P4168834546" "You have Numina trapped in a... Soul Catcher?<br><br><color orange>Toph Osir's eyes flare jealously at the power in your possession.</color><br><br>This is greater fortune than I had hoped for..."
// Answer Text :
"P3263811342" "Numina is mine, Toph. Don't sour our deal with greed."
// Page BetrayalPage2 Text :
"P4123940609" "Greed?<br><br>GREED!?<br><br>That Soul Catcher was stolen from my people by that wizard, Mortimer Kal! It shall be ours again!"
// Answer Text :
"P1848841000" ""Over my dead body." (Fight)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3766735065" "<color yellow>Tammy Arcanus</color>, also known as the hero, <color red>Numina</color>, is the first key that you will require to gain access to Positron's Laboratory. She is the ghost whose voice you must use to open the gate to your destiny. In order to do that you will need to contain her in this.<br><br><color orange>Mortimer Kal produces a foot long length of roughly hewn red crystal from inside an unseen pocket within his robes and extends it to you.</color><br><br>It is a <color yellow>Soul Catcher</color>, and with it you will be able to steal away Numina's spiritual essence and seal it within this artifact. </color yellow>Numina has been a spirit for a long time, {HeroName}, and she may have to be significantly weakened before the Soul Catcher can contain her.</color><br><br>Once Numina's soul is trapped within she will do as you command. Her voice will open the doors to Positron's Laboratory.<br><br>Would you like me to locate Ms. Arcanus for you?"
// AcceptString :
"P245587996" "Find Numina, wizard."
// SendOffString :
"P1056848450" "<color orange>Mortimer Kal's eyes roll back into his head. The sight of the old man standing before you like that reminds you of a zombie, except that he speaks with a gravely tone and mentions nothing about brains.</color><br><br>Numina is currently engaged in battle deep beneath the earth in the forgotten city of <color yellow>Oranbega</color>, the forlorn realm of the Circle of Thorns. But be wary, for with her is her protege, the demon binding warrior <color red>Infernal</color>. The Soul Catcher can only contain the soul of one being at a time, and Infernal will not look kindly upon you for trapping his mentor. You will have to find a way to deal with Infernal for he will stop at nothing to release his mistress.<br><br><color orange>Mortimer Kal smiles</color><br><br>K'Varr is part of Infernal's true name. A person's true name holds power over them. This will give you the edge you need to defeat Numina's protector."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3080569691" "Steal Numina's soul!"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1072176834" "Numina and Infernal are currently embattled with the Circle of Thorns deep inside Oranbega. I will transport you there through a doorway between shadows.<br><br><color yellow>Remember, Numina may initially be too strong to contain within the Soul Catcher, you may have to weaken her before it can take effect.</color>"
// TaskTitle :
"P2931932731" "<color deepskyblue>The Fire and The Flames</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1743778465" "<color deepskyblue>Part 1: The Voice Of A Ghost</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3758459274" "According to Mortimer Kal, Numina and her sidekick, Infernal, are down here in Oranbega fighting the Circle of Thorns. Following their wake of destruction should make your job of tracking the ethereal Numina oh so much easier."
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3899625313" "Speak with Toph Osir"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P269216299" "Return to Toph Osir and speak with him"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P1142348848" "Defeat Toph Osir"
// Script Variable BOSS_1_DISPLAYNAME :
"P810432801" "Agony Mage"
// Script Variable BOSS1_DISPLAYINFO :
"P856364347" ""
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1347042829" "<shout>Our city is under attack by that accursed Infernal and his keeper, Numina!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4028364830" "<shout>{HeroName}!?<em>Come thinking to steal treasures from our city in the wake of our misfortune?<em>Think again!"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P86128632" "<shout><em t=5>But what are we to do? So long as Infernal runs rampant the daemons will not obey our summons!"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4230106246" "<shout><em t=5>Kill {Hero.gender=male him|her}!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3177773160" "Hello there."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"
// Script Variable ACTOR1_NAME :
"P574334931" "Guide"
// Script Variable ACTOR5_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1563506336" "Kill!"
// Script Variable ACTOR13_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4153105488" "Up, Thorn brothers. On your feet."
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3700221" "<shout>Get them onto their feet."
// Script Variable BOSS_1_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2668374062" "<shout>Excellent!<em>An opportunity to claim new bodies for our fallen brothers!"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1025490693" "<shout><em t=3>Rise, brethren. This fight has only just begun."
// Script Variable BOSS_2_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2654129257" "<shout><em t=5>Capture them alive!"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2634516415" "...ugh...<em>...can't... stand."
// Script Variable ACTOR7_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4212582949" "<em t=3>This accursed body is weakened."
// Script Variable ACTOR7_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2670401564" "But it is not yet dead!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1699779266" "<shout>Once we've recovered we are only to prevent them from escaping."
// Script Variable BOSS_1_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4186068561" "<shout>Come to Oranbega to die, have we, {HeroName}?"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4274748052" "<shout><em t=5>Without our daemon allies that will prove more difficult."
// Script Variable BOSS_2_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2711924166" "<shout><em t=4>Destroy the intruders!"
// Script Variable ACTOR1_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3963644943" "My... strength... returns!"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4278347246" "Not... dead... yet!"
// Script Variable ACTOR10_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1462289923" "Pain is strength!"
// Script Variable ACTOR11_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3212410569" "This body is but a vessel!"
// Script Variable ACTOR15_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1876335926" "I've strength yet!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3456251770" "<shout>We must focus our efforts on Infernal.<em>Thousands of daemons are trapped in his armor, releasing them would surely gain us great favor and power with the daemon lords."
// Script Variable BOSS_2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3908599974" "<em t=8><shout>No!<em>Numina is the true threat!<em>Infernal can lay low our bodies but the daughter of Arcanus can keep us bound within them, and enslaved to her will!"
// Script Variable BOSS_3_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P237772941" "<em t=15><shout>All that exists is her spirit, pain is no longer a concern of hers.<em>I can find no means of forcing her into a host body to contain her."
// Script Variable BOSS_4_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2872100600" "<em t=22><shout>There are other ways to deal with that phantasm that vexes us so.<em>A soul unbound can be imprisoned in more than just bodies..."
// Script Variable BOSS_1_DISPLAYNAME :
"P108261530" "Blade Prince"
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P159099138" "<em t=5><shout>You will be SILENT,  Berith!<em>You do not speak for us all."
// Script Variable BOSS_2_DISPLAYNAME :
"P111718010" "Behemoth Lord"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P992805814" "<shout>So long as Infernal is here we shall NOT aid the Circle!"
// Script Variable BOSS_3_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1866627069" "<em t=10><shout>Ayperos is right...<em>But Berith speaks of our true problem.<em>Infernal."
// Script Variable BOSS_4_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3278585935" "<em t=16><shout>If Infernal could be imprisoned then the last of the Arcanus blood line would soon be ours!"
// Script Variable BOSS_5_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2895581136" "<em t=23><shout>Yes, we must convince the Oranbegans that it is Infernal, not Tammy Arcanus, who must be dealt with first."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3115389772" "Toph Osir"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2055576523" "<shout>{HeroName}. Cease your attack and let us speak civilly."
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P4072648281" "This day I achieve three great victories with one stroke!"
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1459814055" "You think pain bothers me? This body is just a vessel for my immortal soul!"
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3157790802" "Impossible! How is it that you can resist my magic so?"
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1088188639" "My... My spells... They are coming undone..."
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P3027179555" "You... Fool! Now Infernal... is... free..."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P195121789" "<em victory>When next you see Mortimer Kal rest assured that it will be in hell!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2967153691" "Perhaps if we work together we can both have what we want."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2002440868" "<shout>I am Toph Osir, Magus of this district of our glorious city.<em>You are not here on the same mission as Numina and her pet, Infernal... what is it you seek?<em>Perhaps I can grant what you wish in exchange for your assistance against that witch, Numina?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P432828994" "<shout>So it would seem that the threads of Fate have brought us together.<em>Numina has been using her magic to turn my people against each other.<em>Normally this would pose little problem for our daemons to handle, but that accursed Infernal is with her, and what daemons we have sent against them have been bound within his armor.<em>If we could but separate one from the other then both would fall."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1344014650" "<shout>Of course! K'Varr is part of Infernal's true name.<em>It isn't absolute power over him, but it is enough to summon him away from his mistress and to a place where he can be bound.<em>Once we have Infernal imprisoned I will leave Numina to your capable hands."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P4030970319" "<shout>With Infernal bound by his name and my spell, Numina should prove no threat to you.<em>Once you have dealt with her return to me and I will grant you safe passage from our city.<em>But, if I find that your true motive is to steal from my people, then know that there is no respite for thieves within the hallowed walls of Oranbega."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P437620075" "<shout>You have Numina trapped in a... Soul Catcher?<em>This is greater fortune than I had hoped for..."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P328683893" "<shout>MWAH HA HA HA HAAAA!<em>Ah... Infernal.<em>Finally we meet face to face.<em>Or should I call you...<em>K'Varr.<em>Soon the entirety of your true name will be known to me...<em>And then it is I, Toph Osir, who shall command the daemons bound within your armor...<em>For you shall be under MY command!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P555867741" "<shout>Kill {HeroName} and bring Numina's soul to me!"

